# Line endings.
#
# GitHub's Windows runners set `core.autocrlf=true`, so without this file a
# Windows checkout rewrites every text file to CRLF. That is invisible on Linux
# and macOS and breaks exactly the tests that treat a file as *bytes*:
# `tests/mail_hostile_message.rs` compares the checked-in sanitizer fixture
# against the pipeline's own output, and a CRLF copy of it can never match.
# Pin the working tree to LF on every platform instead of teaching each such
# test to normalize — the byte-for-byte comparison is the point of those tests,
# and LF is what the green Linux/macOS runs have always fed them, `.eml`
# message fixtures included.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Consumed by cmd.exe, which wants CRLF.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
